 "_note": "`on:frame` as data: the display-link contract folded from raw platform ticks and lifecycle events. An always-running frame callback is a BATTERY BUG, so the law is enforced by fixture, not by intent. (1) The loop is installed ONLY while an `on:frame` handler is bound AND the canvas is mounted AND it is on screen \u2014 the corpus counts `installs`/`uninstalls`, so a renderer that installs a display link for an unbound canvas fails here. (2) Ticks arriving while the loop is not installed are DROPPED, never queued. (3) The emitted payload is { time, delta, frame }: `delta` is seconds since the previous EMITTED tick and is 0 on the first tick after every install; `time` is accumulated delta, so it EXCLUDES offscreen intervals (an author animating from `time` must not see a jump after backgrounding); `frame` counts emissions and never resets while mounted. (4) The 60/s budget: a tick arriving less than 1000/60 ms after the last EMITTED tick is coalesced away \u2014 the same constant the scene kernel uses, deliberately shared.",
